# Media Format Specification
This document defines the required technical standards for all media assets used in the
Football Coaching App. These rules ensure consistency, fast loading, accessibility, and
predictable rendering across devices.

---

## 1. IMAGE FORMATS

### Pitch Layout Diagrams
- Format: PNG
- Aspect Ratio: **4:5 (preferred)** or **1:1 (acceptable)**
- Resolution: Minimum 800px on the short edge
- Background: Clean, minimal, high contrast
- Style: Consistent icons, colours, arrows, and line weights
- Naming: pitch-u9-session-001.png
- Storage Path: `/media/pitch-diagrams/u9/`

### Video Thumbnails
- Format: PNG
- Aspect Ratio: **16:9**
- Resolution: Minimum 1280×720
- Purpose: Fast-loading preview for demo videos
- Naming: thumb-u9-session-001.png
- Storage Path: `/media/video-thumbnails/u9/`

---

## 2. VIDEO FORMATS

### Demo Videos
- Format: MP4 (if self-hosted)
- Codec: H.264 recommended
- Max Length: 30–60 seconds
- Resolution: 720p or 1080p
- Thumbnail Required: Yes (see above)
- Naming: video-u9-session-001.mp4
- Storage Path: `/media/videos/u9/`

### External Hosting (Preferred)
- YouTube or Vimeo URLs may be used instead of MP4 files.
- Only store the URL in the database.
- Thumbnail still required and stored in Supabase.

---

## 3. ACCESSIBILITY REQUIREMENTS

### All images must include:
- `alt_text` describing the diagram or thumbnail
- Example: “Pitch layout showing 3v1 rondo with cones in a square”

### All videos must include:
- `demoVideoCaption` (short description)
- Example: “Demonstration of 3v1 rondo movement and passing pattern”

